# ASRP — Agentic Systematic Review Pipeline

An end-to-end, multi-agent AI system that autonomously conducts PRISMA-2020 systematic literature reviews on any given topic. Built with LangGraph, Groq (LLM), OpenAlex + arXiv (sources), and a hybrid Chroma + BM25 RAG pipeline.

---

## Overview

Systematic literature reviews (SLRs) are methodologically demanding: they require protocol definition, multi-database search, dual screening, structured extraction, quality appraisal, synthesis, and PRISMA-compliant reporting. A single SLR typically takes 6–18 months.

**ASRP** automates this pipeline with 7 autonomous agents coordinated by LangGraph, while preserving transparency (audit trail, decision rationales, verifiable references) and human oversight (interrupts at protocol validation and screening review).

**Demonstration topic:** *"Effects of coffee on cognitive performance"* → 20 records identified, 5 studies included, full narrative synthesis with DOI-verifiable references, produced in ~7 minutes on a free-tier LLM.

---

## Key Features

- **Full PRISMA-2020 workflow** — from protocol generation to final report.
- **7 specialised agents** — planner, search strategist, retrieval, dual screening, extraction, synthesis, critic.
- **Hybrid RAG** — Chroma (dense) + BM25 (sparse) over abstracts, with local `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` embeddings (zero API cost).
- **Dual-reviewer screening** — strict reviewer (model A) + inclusive reviewer (model B), with conflict detection and PRISMA inclusion counts.
- **Deterministic references** — the References section is generated in Python from real OpenAlex/arXiv records (DOI-verifiable), never hallucinated by the LLM.
- **Critic agent** — automatically detects hallucinated citations, missing counts, and protocol violations.
- **Human-in-the-loop** — LangGraph interrupts at protocol validation and after screening.
- **Audit trail** — every decision is traced to `runs/<timestamp>/trace.jsonl` (JSON Lines).
- **Rate-limit resilience** — adaptive TokenBucket (TPM-aware), Groq retry with exact wait-time parsing, and disk cache for crash recovery.

